# Tailwind CSS

This project uses **Tailwind CSS v4**, which is configured in CSS rather than JavaScript.

- There is no `tailwind.config.ts` or `tailwind.config.js`, and one should not be created.
  All configuration lives in `src/app/globals.css` via `@import "tailwindcss"`,
  `@theme`, and `@custom-variant`.
- Design tokens are defined as CSS variables in `globals.css` and exposed through
  `@theme inline`. Add new tokens there rather than inventing one-off values.

## Styling

- Apply utility classes through `className`. Do not add CSS modules or a styling library.
- Reference semantic theme tokens, for example `bg-background`, `text-foreground`,
  `text-muted-foreground`, and `border-input`, instead of literal colors like
  `bg-[#171717]`. This keeps light and dark mode working.
- Merge conditional classes with the `cn()` helper from `@/lib/utils`.
- Write plain CSS in `globals.css` only for genuinely global concerns such as base
  element styles or keyframes.
